## Locked (2026-08-07)

After **`gt submit`** / **`gt submit --stack`**, decide “may enqueue” from
the **Graphite-ready author clone**:

| Prefer | Avoid as primary |
|--------|------------------|
| **`cstack-gt-wait-merge`** (Ready → `gt merge`; Cannot determine + mergeable → tip `merge-queue` label) | Hand-rolled `sleep` + `grep` loops |
| `gt info` / `gt log` → **`(Ready to merge)`** / as stack | Waiting on ignored Vercel rows |
| Poll sleep **5–12s** (default **8s**) | Default **`sleep 20` / `60` / `75` / `180`** |
| Break the loop on affirmative Ready | Fixed `for … sleep` after already green |
| **`Required checks failed` → break + act** (rerun/fix) | Dry-run sleep while already failed |

Still waiting: dry-run not ready / `gt` shows **`(Waiting on CI...)`** with
**no** failed checks.

**`Cannot determine` is not a wait-forever signal.** Do **not** `gt merge`.
The binary syncs once (`--no-restack`), retries, then if required GH
checks are green and `CLEAN`/`UNSTABLE`, labels the **tip** `merge-queue`
and exits 0. That is Graphite’s official enqueue-from-anywhere path.

**Failed ≠ waiting (Chase lock 2026-08-08):** if dry-run says
`Required checks failed` / `Failed CI`, **stop the wait loop immediately**.
Do not keep polling for Ready. Same session: ≤2 `gh run rerun --failed` for
known flake, else minimal CI unblock → `gt submit` → dry-run → merge (or
`HANDOFF: grok-ci-merge`). SoT: `sume-gt-mq` § Ready-signal + § F.

## Repo-wide CI flake (Chase lock 2026-08-07)

Ops detail: **`sume-gt-mq` § F**.

If required Test fails with **shifting timeouts** / same signature on
**unrelated** PRs / local suite green in seconds:

1. **≤2** `gh run rerun` attempts on the same head
2. Then ship a **minimal CI unblock** (e.g. package `testTimeout`) via
   fresh-clone `gt submit` — product scope stays locked
3. **Forbidden:** endless `gh run rerun` with zero code change
4. Still blocked → `HANDOFF: grok-ci-merge`

## Why

Graphite docs: post-submit `gt log` includes PR status
([visualize a stack](https://graphite.com/docs/visualize-stack)); merge
waits on GitHub checks
([merge PRs](https://graphite.com/docs/merge-pull-requests)).  
`gh pr checks` inside Claude tool shells can **401** and also surfaces
non-required noise (`Graphite / mergeability_check`, cancelled Vercel).  
Long sleep defaults lag minutes after the stack is already Ready.

## Fallback only

If `gt` is broken: filter `gh pr view --json statusCheckRollup` to
Format / Typecheck / Test / Build / validate / Graphite CI optimizer.
**401 ≠ pending.** Prefer fix `gt auth` and return to `cstack-gt-wait-merge`.

Cook: **`cstack-gt-wait-merge`** after every `gt submit`. Affirmative Ready
(`Your stack is ready to merge` / `(Ready to merge)` /
`(Ready to merge as stack)`) → `gt merge`. `Cannot determine` + mergeable
→ tip `merge-queue` label. Forbidden: substring grep `ready to merge`.

Keep `sume-chase-work-loop.mdc` + `opus-background-terminal.mdc` GRAPHITE
blocks in sync with **`sume-gt-mq`** + the orchestration delegation checklist.
